# ML Lab Practical 6: ANN on Seeds Dataset

**Author:** Prabhkirat Singh Marwah
**Section:** B | **Batch:** B4 | **Roll No:** 47
**Subject:** Machine Learning Lab | **Practical No.:** 6

## Aim
To build and train an Artificial Neural Network (ANN) that classifies wheat seeds into 3 classes.

## Dataset
`seeds_new.csv`: 7 numerical features, target column `Class (1, 2, 3)`.

## Model
Input (7) → Dense 16 (ReLU) → Dense 8 (ReLU) → Dense 3 (Softmax)

## Settings
Adam (lr = 0.001), Sparse Categorical Crossentropy, up to 100 epochs, batch size 32, validation split 20%, Early Stopping (patience = 10). Data split: 80% train and 20% test, scaled with `StandardScaler`.

## Results
| Accuracy | Precision | Recall | F1 Score |
|----------|-----------|--------|----------|
| 88.10% | 0.8995 | 0.8810 | 0.8731 |

## How to Run
1. `pip install numpy pandas matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn tensorflow`
2. Keep `seeds_new.csv` next to `Untitled13.ipynb`.
3. Run all cells in order.

## Conclusion
The ANN classified the seed types with 88.10% test accuracy.
